    body: `
For years, TV commercials felt out of reach for most local companies. They meant big production budgets, broad audiences you couldn't control, and a media bill that only national brands could stomach. That has changed. **Streaming TV advertising for local business** now puts your message on the same living-room screens as the big brands, with the kind of targeting you'd expect from digital ads. Here's how it works, what drives the cost, and how to make every impression count.

## Why Streaming TV Is the Biggest Shift in Television Advertising in Decades

Viewers haven't stopped watching TV. They've just changed *how* they watch. Many households now stream through smart TVs, streaming sticks and gaming consoles instead of a traditional cable box. As those viewers moved, advertising followed them, and the old rules went away along the way.

Traditional TV sells time slots. You buy a spot during the evening news and hope the right people are watching. Streaming sells *audiences*. You decide who should see your ad, and the platform delivers it to those households. For a local business, that's the difference between paying to reach an entire metro area and paying to reach the neighborhoods you actually serve.

## CTV vs. OTT vs. Broadcast and Cable: What Each Term Actually Means

The jargon can be confusing, so here's a quick rundown:

- **CTV (Connected TV):** The device, meaning a TV connected to the internet. Smart TVs, streaming sticks and consoles all count.
- **OTT (Over-the-Top):** Streaming content delivered over the internet instead of through a cable or satellite provider. OTT can be watched on a TV, phone, tablet or laptop.
- **Broadcast:** Traditional over-the-air TV from local stations, bought by market and time slot.
- **Cable:** Programming delivered through a cable or satellite subscription, often available in smaller geographic zones than broadcast.

In practice, "CTV" usually means OTT ads watched on the big screen. That's the premium spot you want.

## How Streaming Ads Let You Target by Zip Code, Interest, and Household

This is where streaming really earns its place. Instead of buying a whole market, you can narrow delivery by:

- **Geography:** Zip codes, radiuses or custom areas around your business
- **Demographics:** Age ranges, household income and family composition
- **Interests and behaviors:** Homebuyers, outdoor enthusiasts, recent movers and more
- **Retargeting:** Households that have already visited your website

Precise targeting only helps if you know who you're targeting. If you haven't defined your ideal customer yet, start with [market research for small business](https://onetakewondermarketing.com/blog/market-research-for-small-business-know-your-customer) before you spend a dollar.

## What Streaming TV Advertising Really Costs (And Why the Minimum Spend Is Lower Than You Think)

Streaming is usually priced on a **CPM**, the cost per thousand impressions. Because you're only paying to reach the households you chose, very little of your budget is spent on viewers who will never become customers.

Your actual cost depends on how tightly you target, which networks and apps you run on, the season, and how long your campaign runs. Unlike traditional TV, you don't need a massive upfront commitment to get started. Campaigns can be sized to fit a local business budget and scaled up once you see what's working. For more on stretching your budget, read our guide to [marketing on a budget](https://onetakewondermarketing.com/blog/marketing-on-a-budget).

## Creative That Works on the Big Screen: Length, Format, and Non-Skippable Spots

Many streaming ads are **non-skippable**, so viewers see your whole message. That's a big opportunity, and it means a weak ad gets noticed too. A few best practices:

- **Keep it tight.** 15- and 30-second spots are the standard. Say one thing well.
- **Hook early.** Make the first few seconds count visually.
- **Brand clearly.** Show your logo and name early and again at the end.
- **Design for a big screen.** Use clean visuals, readable text and good sound.
- **End with one clear action.** Visit, call or search, but pick only one.

Strong creative makes everything else work better. Learn more about why [video is the highest-converting asset](https://onetakewondermarketing.com/blog/video-production-for-business-marketing-that-sells) in your marketing mix.

## Measuring Streaming Campaigns: Completion Rates, Site Visits, and Attribution

Streaming gives you much more data than traditional TV. Key metrics include:

- **Completion rate:** How many viewers watched your ad all the way through
- **Reach and frequency:** How many households saw it, and how often
- **Site visits:** Households that saw your ad and later visited your website
- **Conversions:** Calls, form fills or purchases tied back to exposure

Attribution isn't perfect, but it's a huge step up from guessing. For the bigger picture, see [how to measure marketing ROI](https://onetakewondermarketing.com/blog/measure-marketing-roi).

## When to Pair Streaming with Broadcast, Cable, and Digital in One Media Plan

Streaming works best as part of a team. Broadcast and cable still deliver broad reach for big local moments. Streaming adds precision. [PPC](https://onetakewondermarketing.com/blog/ppc-advertising-paid-search-guide) and [social media advertising](https://onetakewondermarketing.com/blog/social-media-advertising-for-small-business) catch people when they're ready to act. When someone sees your ad on TV and searches for you later, you want to show up. Not sure where each channel fits? Our breakdown of [TV advertising vs. digital ads](https://onetakewondermarketing.com/blog/tv-advertising-vs-digital-ads) can help.

## Common Mistakes Businesses Make Buying Streaming Ads on Their Own

- **Buying cheap inventory without knowing where it runs.** Some "CTV" ends up on phones or low-quality apps.
- **Targeting too broadly or too narrowly.** Either one wastes budget.
- **Running too few impressions.** Frequency builds recognition.
- **Reusing creative that wasn't made for TV.** A vertical social clip won't look right on a 65-inch screen.
- **Not connecting measurement.** Without tracking, you can't prove anything.
- **Sending viewers to a weak website.** Interest disappears if your site doesn't convert. Read up on [web design that converts](https://onetakewondermarketing.com/blog/web-design-that-turns-visitors-into-customers).

These are exactly the reasons [professional media buying](https://onetakewondermarketing.com/blog/professional-media-buying-roi-diy-advertising) tends to outperform do-it-yourself buying.

## How We Plan and Buy Streaming TV That Proves Its ROI

At One Take Wonder Marketing, we don't just place ads. We start with your goals and budget, then build a plan around them. We define your audience, choose quality inventory, help produce creative made for the big screen, and connect measurement so you can see what your investment is doing. Because we handle media buying, TV and streaming, digital, creative and web design under one roof, every piece works together.

**Streaming TV advertising for local business** isn't just for big brands anymore. With the right strategy, it can be one of the most effective ways to get your name in front of the households that matter most to you.

**Ready to see your business on the big screen?** [Let's chat](https://onetakewondermarketing.com/contact) or call us at **(321) 483-8762** to start building a streaming campaign that proves its worth.
